上次结果 = -2147024894 = 0x80070002 = ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND. The S4U run failed! Probably because the Command field has quoted exe + quoted arg combined — Task Scheduler's Command should be just the exe, with Arguments separate. In XML, `<Command>` with embedded quoted args may not parse under /xml create. role-clock used a .cmd with no args. Fix: XML with <Command>python.exe path</Command><Arguments>...</Arguments>, or simpler: create a wrapper .cmd like role-clock does (kdo-vault-git-backup.cmd) — consistent with existing pattern and avoids quoting issues.

  Also note: S4U runs in session 0 — python at "C:\Program Files\Python312\python.exe" accessible. Use wrapper cmd:

  @echo off
  cd /d C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\wiki
  "C:\Program Files\Python312\python.exe" kdo-tools\vault_git_backup.py >> logs\vault-git-backup.log 2>&1

